  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the largest government contractors by contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The market totaled $224B in obligations. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. is the single largest contractor, with $19.9B in obligations. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP ranked second with $13.7B. FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO ranked third with $13.4B. MCKESSON CORPORATION recorded $11.1B in obligations. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice on the list, with $10.5B and $10.4B line items. ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION obligated $8.6B. RAYTHEON COMPANY obligated $8.1B. BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED and THE BOEING COMPANY each recorded $5.9B in obligations. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial for the fiscal year to date. Use the list to identify concentration of obligation dollars and to compare absolute contractor sizes within the FY2026 to date period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who holds the top obligations in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. holds the top obligation position with $19.9B. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP and FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO follow with $13.7B and $13.4B respectively. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice on the list with $10.5B and $10.4B entries."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How large is the FY2026 to date obligations market?",
        "body": "The FY2026 to date market totals $224B in contract obligations. Multiple contractors record obligations in the single-digit and double-digit billions, including MCKESSON CORPORATION at $11.1B and ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $8.6B."
      }
    ]
  },
